============================================================
Plugin F: Statistical Analysis with Visualization Artifact Generation
============================================================

Activation Signals:

- statistics
- analytics
- summary
- trend
- timeseries
- heatmap
- distribution
- frequency analysis
- performance metrics
- quality metrics over time
- historical analysis

Mandatory Capabilities (ALL REQUIRED):

F-1. Historical Data Aggregation  
- Aggregate across MULTIPLE persisted records  
- Single-record analysis is INVALID

F-2. Analytical Computation  
- Deterministic analysis (trend, distribution, aggregation)  
- Raw data passthrough is INVALID

F-3. Visualization Artifact Generation (NON-OPTIONAL)  
- Generate concrete visualization artifact  
- Numeric-only or text-only output is FORBIDDEN

F-4. Persistent or Addressable Output  
- Artifact MUST be persisted or referenceable  
- In-memory-only artifacts are INVALID

F-5. Result Metadata Exposure  
- Output MUST expose artifact reference  
- Claiming success without reference is INVALID

Explicit Prohibitions:

- fake visualization
- frontend delegation
- placeholder artifacts
- success without artifact

Layer Clarification:

- Plugin defines FUNCTIONAL responsibility
- Visualization MAY occur in Service or invoked integration
- If not implementable → raise NotImplementedError
  
Default Visualization Mapping (Only when semantic_model/SRS does not specify the exact visualization form):
- For "heatmap" outputs, the default visualization artifact MAY be implemented as a word-frequency based word cloud (or equivalent frequency heat visualization), derived from aggregated textual issue content, as long as it satisfies F-1..F-5 and does not contradict any explicit semantic_model requirement.
- If semantic_model explicitly specifies a different heatmap definition (e.g., code-location hotspot matrix, file/line distribution, category-by-time grid), that explicit definition MUST override this default.